      "content": "No, I wouldn't recommend crushing and administering adult Tylenol to your child. Adult tablets are much too large and may cause choking if your child tries to swallow them whole. Consult with your pediatrician for guidance on using adult Tylenol for children, and they can provide you with the correct dosage based on your child's weight and age. It's always best to use pediatric-strength medications specifically formulated for children.",
